{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcvYJbRje628Mwk3mPBf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011B4CXs7wG8Q4gxxo7WCKzR","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"done","summary":"JMAK devices can now receive commands over TCP and over SMS. The new class is `JmakProtocolEncoder(Protocol, boolean textChannel)`, and `JmakProtocol` registers it for both data and text commands. Over TCP a command is written `$<id>;<value>;|...#`. Over SMS it is written `JMAK#<s|e>;<id>;<value>#...`, and reboot is the literal `JMAK#REBOOT#`. Your examples come out exactly as you gave them. The full test suite and checkstyle pass when run with JDK 25. Two points to know. First, the task text had a broken spot where the TCP prefix should be; I used `$`, taken from your example `$34;1;#`. Second, Traccar has no 'movement alarm' command type. I used `alarmGeofence` for it, because the Meiligao encoder already sends its movement alarm through that type.","changes":[{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/JmakProtocolEncoder.java","summary":"New encoder for custom, engine stop and resume, output control (index 1/2/3 maps to parameters 34/94/167), periodic positions, odometer, set connection (parameter 13 for an IPv4 address, 43 for a domain, then 12 for the port), reboot, speed limit, low battery alarm, power removal alarm and movement alarm (alarmGeofence, parameter 59). Builds the TCP or SMS format depending on textChannel."},{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/JmakProtocol.java","summary":"Declares the supported data and text commands, sets the SMS encoder (textChannel=true), and adds StringEncoder and the TCP encoder (textChannel=false) to the pipeline."},{"path":"src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/JmakProtocolEncoderTest.java","summary":"Tests every supported command over TCP and over SMS, including the examples from the task."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"Commands encoded as described over TCP and SMS","met":true,"evidence":"JmakProtocolEncoderTest passes. It checks `$43;jmak.com.br;|12;5259;#`, `JMAK#s;13;191.233.246.121#s;12;5259#`, `JMAK#e;57;0#`, `$34;1;#`, `JMAK#REBOOT#`, `$93;1;#` and every other supported command in both modes."},{"criterion":"Change covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"New JmakProtocolEncoderTest has two tests: testEncodeData for TCP and testEncodeSms for SMS."},{"criterion":"Existing test suite still passes","met":true,"evidence":"With JAVA_HOME set to JDK 25, `./gradlew checkstyleMain checkstyleTest test` ended in BUILD SUCCESSFUL. The test results show 612 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors and 27 skipped."}],"human_needed":[{"question":"Which command type should the JMAK movement alarm (parameter 59) use? I used Command.TYPE_ALARM_GEOFENCE, with the value from KEY_DATA.","why":"Command.java has no movement alarm type. Meiligao uses alarmGeofence for its movement alarm, but alarmVibration or a new type would also make sense."},{"question":"Is the TCP prefix really `$`?","why":"In the task text, the TCP prefix was replaced by garbled text. I took `$` from the example `$34;1;#`."}],"harness_used":["Skill .claude/skills/add-protocol-decoder: its steps for adding an encoder and registering supported commands","Existing encoders used as patterns: WondexProtocol/WondexProtocolEncoder (text command encoder registration), MeiligaoProtocolEncoder (movement alarm mapped to alarmGeofence), WatchProtocolEncoder (KEY_ENABLE for alarms)","src/test/java/org/traccar/ProtocolTest.java verifyEncode helper"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":".claude/skills/add-protocol-decoder/SKILL.md","problem":"The skill says to use `make test TESTS=...` and `make check-fast`, but this worktree has no Makefile. I used `./gradlew test --tests ...` and `./gradlew checkstyleMain checkstyleTest test` instead."},{"file":"build.gradle","problem":"The build needs Java 21 or newer (`invalid source release: 21`), but the default JDK on the machine is 17, and nothing in the repo says 